  "term": "dogmatism",
  "definition": "Dogmatism is a philosophical stance that begins from accepted principles rather than proving them first. In a broader sense, it refers to uncritical thinking that relies on unnecessary assumptions, and it has also been used for the pre-Kantian philosophy associated especially with Christian Wolff.",
